/* Tutorial window */
"tutorial.title" = "How to Use fi-6110 Scanner";
"tutorial.intro" = "This guide shows you, step by step, how to digitize your documents with the Fujitsu fi-6110 scanner.";
"tut.connect.t" = "Connect the scanner";
"tut.connect.b" = "Connect the scanner to your Mac with the USB cable and turn it on. When the dot at the top right turns green, the scanner is ready. If it stays orange, check the cable and that it's powered on, then wait a few seconds.";
"tut.load.t" = "Load the pages";
"tut.load.b" = "Put the sheets in the automatic feeder, text facing you and the top edge down. You can load several sheets at once: they'll be scanned one after another.";
"tut.options.t" = "Choose the options";
"tut.options.b" = "On the right, choose the kind (color, grayscale or black & white), the resolution in dpi (higher means more detail but larger files) and the paper size. Turn on “Scan both sides” to capture both faces in a single pass.";
"tut.format.t" = "Choose the file format";
"tut.format.b" = "“PDF” makes a single document with all pages. “PDF (searchable)” adds text recognition, so you can search and copy the words in the document. JPEG, PNG and TIFF instead make one image per page.";
"tut.extras.t" = "Handy options";
"tut.extras.b" = "“Rotate pages automatically” detects a sheet fed upside-down and turns it the right way up. “Straighten pages automatically” corrects sheets that went in slightly skewed. “Skip blank pages” drops empty backsides when scanning both sides.";
"tut.arrange.t" = "Rearrange the pages";
"tut.arrange.b" = "After scanning you can drag the pages to change their order, or press “Reverse order” to reverse it. “Flip all” rotates every page 180° at once. Double-click a page to rotate it 180°; right-click it to rotate right, left, flip it, or delete it (the app asks first). The saved file is updated automatically.";
"tut.append.t" = "Add scans to an existing PDF";
"tut.append.b" = "Want to add sheets to a PDF you already have? Press “Add to a PDF” on the right (or the button on the opening screen) and choose the document: its pages appear in the window with a PDF badge, and the sheets you scan are added at the end. The original document's pages are copied untouched, text included. The app saves the result onto the PDF you picked: if you'd rather not replace it, switch off “Overwrite the file if it already exists” and a new file is created instead. Press “Scan” again and the app asks whether to add the new sheets at the end or redo the scan. With a PDF loaded, the two buttons at the top act on the newly scanned pages only: the original document's pages never move and never turn. You can still turn a single PDF page with a double-click or the right-click menu.";
"tut.save.t" = "Where the files go";
"tut.save.b" = "Under “Save to” pick the folder (usually Documents). “Name” already contains today's date: change it however you like. If a file with the same name already exists, a new one is created with -1, -2… added, without overwriting the old one. Turn on “Overwrite the file if it already exists” if you'd rather replace it.";
"tut.defaults.t" = "Set your defaults";
"tut.defaults.b" = "From “fi-6110 Scanner ▸ Settings…” (⌘,) you can choose the options you want ready every time you open the app: kind, resolution, both sides, format and more.";
"tut.trouble.t" = "If something goes wrong";
"tut.trouble.b" = "“Scanner not found”: check the USB cable and that the scanner is on. “Paper jam”: open the scanner, remove the sheets and try again. Remember to load the sheets in the feeder before pressing “Scan”.";
